{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371783-demons-cover-and-arcana","id":371783,"title":"Demons, Cover, and Arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-15T21:19:54-08:00","id":371783,"title":"Demons, Cover, and Arcana","content":"I put this here because it really requires an extensive knowledge of demon, but to a lesser degree (but only slightly lesser) Mage, rather than vice-versa.<br /> <br /> This is not a question of &quot;how do I counter a demons powers,&quot; I actually detest Mages stomping on all the other supes. But there is a question of how to <i>affect</i> a demon that I'm curious about. And I know it will come up sooner or later.<br /> <br /> So, if a demon is in her cover, I assume that's mostly life. I can heal her, I can harm her, I can &quot;buff&quot; her. Since the cover feigns a human and humans are affecting by the Life arcanum, that just seems common sense.<br /> <br /> However, when in their demonic form, things are different. Everywhere I read, it speaks of them as semi-spiritual beings. But they aren't the spirits of the Shadow. And they aren't ghosts. So my question is, what arcanum would one use to affect them in that form? Is it still Life? (Demons are at all times their demonic form <i>and</i> a conglomerate of their covers, due to their quantum states). Is it spirit? (which would be odd, since they aren't Shadow natives) Is it Death? (Seems really unlikely but I'm just postulating, here) Or are they just unable to <i>directly </i>affect them in that form, being outside of the purview of Atlantean magics? (much as the Inferno demons are).<br /> <br /> And I suppose the same question would apply for Angels, should those be encountered. (And while we're on it, can you affect an angel's cover with Life? Are their covers as &quot;streamlined&quot; as a demon's, or is that an effect of Primum?)<br /> <br /> Just wondering if this is already covered somewhere and I'm just missing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T23:00:37-08:00","id":371950,"title":"","content":"Prime would be my guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T23:13:34-08:00","id":371981,"title":"","content":"Per Dave's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/314-stop-gap-god-machine-mechanics-for-mage\">stopgaps</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Targeting an Angel, its Numina, rewriting the Pattern of someone claimed, etc, requires equal parts Prime and Spirit. Angels cannot be summoned. You can try to force one to act in a certain way, but angels are inflexible - if carrying out your wishes conflicts with carrying out the God-Machine's wishes, the Angel's programming wins and the spell has no effect.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:blue\">Or, put another way, God has rolled more successes than you on &quot;angel brainwashing&quot;. Also, no creating members of another major template (by making angels Fall!) without Archmastery. Bad mages, go to back of class</span><br /> <br /> Similarly, Supernal magic can create or manipulate resonance and anchors (and there are several spells in the line to do both already), but can't sense or manipulate Infrastructure at all. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}